    {
      "modelVersion": "gemini-2.5-flash",
      "content": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "text": "Gracias por la aclaración. Entiendo que la interpretación clínica de \"variación estacional\" se refiere a las estaciones del año (Primavera, Verano, Otoño, Invierno) en lugar de meses individuales. He corregido la consulta SQL para agrupar los diagnósticos de náuseas por estas estaciones.\n\nAquí tienes la consulta SQL SELECT corregida y ejecutable para BigQuery:\n\n```sql\nSELECT\n    CASE\n        WHEN EXTRACT(MONTH FROM co.condition_start_date) BETWEEN 3 AND 5 THEN 'Spring'\n        WHEN EXTRACT(MONTH FROM co.condition_start_date) BETWEEN 6 AND 8 THEN 'Summer'\n        WHEN EXTRACT(MONTH FROM co.condition_start_date) BETWEEN 9 AND 11 THEN 'Autumn'\n        ELSE 'Winter'\n    END AS season,\n    COUNT(co.condition_occurrence_id) AS diagnosis_count\nFROM\n    `condition_occurrence` AS co\nWHERE\n    co.condition_concept_id = 31967\nGROUP BY\n    season\nORDER BY\n    CASE season\n        WHEN 'Spring' THEN 1\n        WHEN 'Summer' THEN 2\n        WHEN 'Autumn' THEN 3\n        WHEN 'Winter' THEN 4\n    END;\n```",
            "thoughtSignature": "CqYBAY89a19pffWxiSJlgPv8caY0PsaP7yLa5Q5pcw3_bBDJX_BF31WiFqX4mzf3Zg2ZEO52luV7j96Xw7jB3i42emxnDNrLcl6BR8-OgqmOYGx7m_EI47vJkfPF0FcBTKd0upQ1GdxPk0C_Xl1U9GXbnXodoSD2_H7PuYqmAgm1cAFgRuk97w5DiuJEd8qcS9gMfQkhQb_K06Y2Elt9c9GbRDT5nN-GeQ=="
